================ HOUSE MANAGEMENT API =================

House stores shared property information: location, house number/name, host, agent,
payment duration, total room count, description, services, documents, coordinates,
payment methods, rating, reviews, and optional images. Room stores rental-specific
information: payment duration, price, houseType, clientId, clientName, clientPhone,
and status. Create the house first, then add rooms using the houseId returned by
the house create endpoint.

Database columns added:
- house.total_rooms (API name: totalRooms): count of rooms attached to the house.
  It is initialized for existing houses and maintained automatically when rooms
  are created or deleted.
- room.payment_duration (API name: paymentDuration): rental period in months for
  that room. It is copied automatically from the house paymentDuration when a
  room is created, and existing rooms are synchronized when the house duration
  is updated. Clients do not provide this field when creating or updating rooms.

====> Register a new house by role HOST, AGENT and ADMIN
When the frontend has multiple images, send them in the `images` array in this request. The backend saves the house, uses the first image's `base64Data` as the primary `imageUrl`, then saves the remaining images with their categories against the newly created house ID. The frontend makes one request; it does not need to call the image upload endpoint separately for these images. `imageUrl` remains supported for clients sending only one primary image.
